WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.381
Safe process execution in Python means launching external programs only
when necessary and doing so with explicit trust boundaries.

2
00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:22.013
The application should know who requested the work, which operation is
approved, which executable will run, which arguments are data, which files
may be touched, which environment values are passed, which account is
used, and how success or failure will be handled.

3
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:27.566
Without that clarity, process execution can quietly become an unsafe
operating-system interface.

4
00:00:27.566 --> 00:00:36.711
The strongest designs avoid shell interpretation, separate executable
paths from structured arguments, and map user choices to allowlisted
internal operations.

5
00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:43.112
They validate inputs for type, format, length, range, and business intent,
but they do not rely on validation alone.

6
00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:55.131
They also constrain file paths, set working directories deliberately, use
safe temporary files, minimize inherited environment variables, protect
secrets, and avoid placing sensitive values in arguments or logs.

7
00:00:55.131 --> 00:00:57.744
Runtime controls complete the security story.

8
00:00:57.744 --> 00:01:07.020
Child processes should run with least privilege, appropriate isolation,
limited filesystem and network access, timeouts, output limits, and
concurrency controls.

9
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:16.818
Logs should preserve enough evidence for operations and security review
without exposing secrets, sensitive arguments, private file contents, or
excessive internal detail.

10
00:01:16.818 --> 00:01:21.325
Tests and monitoring should cover failure paths, not just successful
execution.

11
00:01:21.325 --> 00:01:25.898
The practical takeaway is simple: treat process execution as a security
boundary.

12
00:01:25.898 --> 00:01:29.490
Prefer libraries or platform APIs when they can do the job safely.

13
00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:35.304
When external execution is necessary, make it predictable, constrained,
observable, and recoverable.

14
00:01:35.304 --> 00:01:41.640
That approach supports business automation without turning Python
applications into broad command interfaces.
